The `[server]` layer now has signing keys and access tokens. Keys are asymmetric and generated when the `server` profile is applied, never shipped: a key inside the package would be the same key in every site running it. Only the public halves are published, as a JWKS. The ring keeps the previous keys so a rotation does not invalidate tokens that are still inside their lifetime, and it is bounded so the record cannot grow forever. Access tokens are self-encoded JWTs, so issuing one writes nothing to the database; the issuer is configured rather than derived from the portal URL, because relying parties compare it byte for byte. @ericof
